# TypeScript And Aliases

- All application code must be written in TypeScript (`.ts` / `.tsx`).
- Avoid creating new JavaScript source files (`.js` / `.jsx`) in `src`.
- Use one path alias per module root in `tsconfig.json` (e.g. `@api`, `@services`). Do not add duplicate entries such as `@api` and `@api/*` for the same root.
- Import from each layer's `index.ts` barrel (`@api`, `@services`, `@components`, `@templates`, `@i18n`, `@atoms`, etc.), not from deep file paths under those folders.
- Avoid deep relative paths like `../../../` when a barrel alias exists.
- Within the same package (e.g. `services/ai/hooks` importing `services/ai/agentGuardrails`), prefer relative imports to avoid circular dependencies through the barrel.

## Example

```ts
// ✅
import { useAuth } from "@services";
import type { UserRole } from "@api";
import { AppShell } from "@templates";

// ❌ deep path under an aliased root
import { useAuth } from "@services/auth/hooks/useAuth";
import type { UserRole } from "@api/dto/auth/AuthDto";
```
